.TH SNDPSCFG 8 "June 2014" "Xsan File System"
.SH NAME
sndpscfg \- Xsan File System Proxy 
Server Configuration Utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.na
.nh
.HP
.B sndpscfg -e
.HP
.B sndpscfg -E
.I VolName
.HP
.B sndpscfg -a
.ad
.hy
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Xsan File System
\fBsndpscfg\fR command
is a utility used to generate and modify
Proxy Server configuration files on Linux systems.
(NOTE: to view and adjust the Proxy Server settings on 
Windows systems, 
use the LAN Client/Gateway tab in the Client Configuration tool instead.)
.SH SYNTAX
The \fB-e\fP option is used to edit the default \fBdpserver\fP configuration
file.
If no default \fBdpserver\fP file exists, a template file will be generated.
The template file contains commented-out entries for each of the network
interfaces on the system, and commented-out entries for each of the tunable
parameters, specifying default values.
.PP
The \fB-E\fP \fIVolName\fP option is used to edit the file-system-specific
\fBdpserver\fP configuration file for the specified file system.
As with \fB-e\fP, a template file will be generated if no file-system-specific
\fBdpserver\fP file exists.
.PP
The \fB-a\fP option is used to print a template \fBdpserver\fP configuration
file to standard output.
.SH FILES
.I /Library/Preferences/Xsan/dpserver
.br
.I /Library/Preferences/Xsan/dpserver.\fRVolName\fP
